From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:47:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor overlay: ed_overlay_field, a native field overlay (mip
 chain of alpha levels, distance adaptive quadtree, draped, depth tested)

A float field of the field engine can be shown on the ground without Lua touching a sample: ed_overlay_field(id, handle, rgb, maxAlpha, {scale, bias, invert, cutoff,
reduce, px}) keeps the grid (shared pointer), maps it to alpha levels, builds a mip chain (average + maximum) once per handle and mapping, and draws a quadtree of ground
blocks cut up by their projected size (EdOverlayLod.h), each corner carrying the field reduced over the leaf sized box around it, draped (DrapeRect) in the depth tested
ground pass. Blocks with no alpha are dropped, leaves stop at the field's sample size, the tree is built coarser while the camera moves. ed_overlay_perf reports the
field numbers. Pure parts in EdOverlayField.h with EdOverlayFieldTest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

